===Energon Universe===
[[File:TF2023 no. 16 – Devastator and Bruticus duke it out in a forest.JPG|left|300px|thumb]]
After a failed attempt at merging during a battle aboard the downed ''[[Nemesis (G1)|Nemesis]]'', {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 9|Transformers #9}} the Combaticons, after being recruited by Starscream, were finally able to form Bruticus during a battle against Soundwave's team of Decepticons. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 15|Transformers #15}} Not to be outdone, Soundwave ordered the Constructicons to to merge into [[Devastator (G1)#Energon Universe|Devastator]]. The titanic warriors fought as their respective leaders tussled below, all watched from a distance by [[Optimus Prime (G1)#Energon Universe|Optimus Prime]] and the [[Autobot]]s. In a spurt of rage, Prime fired on the Decepticons with his [[fusion cannon]], causing the dam they were fighting on to collapse. Bruticus and Devastator continued their battle even as they were pushed on by the raging river. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 16|Transformers #16}}

Eventually arriving in [[Seattle]], the Decepticons' civil war continued, with Bruticus getting the top of the Space Needle thrown at them by Devastator and receiving an uppercut for good measure. The city itself suffered catastrophic damage during the fight as the Autobots rushed to save as many humans as they could from being crushed underfoot by the grappling giants. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 17|Transformers #17}} Bruticus broke off the fight with Devastator to rescue the downed Starscream, but this distraction allowed Devastator to RKO Bruticus off a skyscraper and into the pavement. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 18|Transformers #18}}

Bruticus was active once again to participate in an all-out assault on the ''[[Ark (G1)|Ark]]'', but his feud with Devastator boiled over once again, and the two began to fight each other instead of the Autobots. [[Megatron (G1)#Energon Universe|Megatron]] managed to straighten them out, but before the two could see who could crush Autobots better, they were taken out of the fight by the newly arrived [[Superion (G1)#energon Universe|Superion]]. The Autobots retreated and Bruticus joined the other Decepticons in pursuit. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 21|Transformers #21}}

[[File:TF2023no29 BulkheadBruticusBam.jpg|thumb|upright=1.5|"Bruticus need to start making better life choices."]]
A human military force intercepted the Decepticons and Bruticus eagerly began slaughtering them, competing with Devastator over how many humans they could kill (Devastator was leading 37-23, much to Bruticus's dismay.) {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 22|Transformers #22}} The Decepticons followed the Autobots to [[Chicago]], where the two forces clashed again and Bruticus joined Devastator in confronting Superion. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 23|Transformers #23}} The fierce battle that followed left Bruticus lying in the rubble, missing his Brawl leg and complaining to Devastator. After Megatron was defeated by Optimus Prime, Bruticus followed Devastator in a retreat, taking a moment to scoop up the near-dead Starscream along the way. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 24|Transformers #24}}

The Combaticons formed Bruticus to fight the Autobots in a forest battle near the ''Ark''. However, Bruticus picked the wrong Autobot to grab and was soon on the receiving end of repeated wrecking ball blows from [[Bulkhead (G1)|Bulkhead]]. Bulkhead grabbed Bruticus by the head and several other Autobots uprooted his leg, toppling the combiner over and forcing the Combaticons to separate. {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 29|Transformers #29}} 

The Combaticons later raided a rural town for energy and were caught in the act by [[Cliffjumper (G1)|Cliffjumper]] and [[Shredhead]].  They formed Bruticus in response and delivered a savage beating to Shredhead.  Cliffjumper managed to stab Bruticus in the neck with Shredhead's sword, forcing the Combaticons to separate and leave the deactivated Onslaught behind as they retreated.  {{storylink|Transformers (2023) issue 34|Transformers #34}}   

