:[[Transformers: Age of the Primes|''Age of the Primes'']] Bruticus is a mostly cartoon-accurate figure (Blast Off chestplate and all, though omitting the brown coloring) that utilizes parts of the frame combiner system devised for ''[[Transformers: Legacy|Legacy]]'' [[Menasor (G1)#Legacy|Menasor]] and later used for ''Age of the Primes'' [[Superion (G1)#Age of the Primes|Superion]], with the limb bots attaching to a skeletal Bruticus formed by Onslaught. Vortex and Blast Off split in half like the arm-bots before them and are even compatible with Superion's arm frame. Where Bruticus significantly differs from the prior frame combiners is with his leg-bots; they form the shins and ankles themselves (while the back of the legs and soles of the feet are still Onslaught's frame) and are thus Voyagers rather than Deluxes to accommodate this.

:As for weaponry, Swindle's trailer converts into a blaster for Bruticus to wield, which can optionally be combined with Swindle's long blaster to form an extended and more toy-accurate rifle. ''Studio Series'' [[Shockwave_(G1)/toys#Studio_Series|Shockwave]] is also capable of transforming into a ''gigantic'' right shoulder cannon for Bruticus, though this is only mentioned in the former's instructions.

:Due to the frame system, Vortex's front half and Blast Off are oriented incorrectly compared to the animation model. Parts of the frame do retain Onslaught's blue and green plastics instead of the cartoon's all grey, though notably the toes have been painted to match Swindle and Brawl.

:Initial CGI renders incorrectly depicted the inside of Bruticus' thighs as unpainted gray (they are painted blue in Onslaught's renders for his vehicle mode as per the final toy), and had Bruticus' gun be entirely black as per an unfinalized deco for Swindle (Swindle's final gun/trailer accessory has yellow sides).
