:Along with the ''T. rex'' [[Grimlock (G1)/toys#DefenderTRex|Grimlock]], the 4th wave of ''[[Blokees]]''' Defender Version line up introduces new vehicle kits of the Combaticons, starting from Brawl, and they also feature similar hardpoints for a Bruticus combiner. In addition to the combiner kibble, Bruticus also comes with an extra open-palm left hand compatible with the feet of any Defender Version kit (especially Starscream) and two-thirds of the sonic stun-gun, as the Onslaught vehicle's chassis is needed to complete the weapon. Unlike the Devastator accessory, Bruticus features newly-tooled shoulder joints that can be raised to compensate for the single shoulder pegs on Blast Off and Vortex in their arm modes, as well as double-jointed knees and ankle joints. Although not documented in the add-on's instructions, the CG stock renders show that Blast Off's elevons can flip inward in Bruticus's arm form.

:Depending on the individual quality of Blast Off's Vehicle kit, the connection between his gestalt upper arm block and the front shuttle's inner frame may detach while attempting to pose in combiner limb form. This can be resolved by gluing the two pieces together, as long as the outer Shuttle kibble is removed beforehand.

: Like Devastator, the add-on was released by redeeming all QR codes from the five cards included with each Combaticon vehicle. This could be done through the Blokees Figures Club app in China or the Blokees app globally. It was eventually also released on the official Blokees website on January 28, 2026.

